      "Title: Common pitfalls in forum navigation and reply submission\nDescription: Key UI signals and potential failure points when interacting with forum comment threads\n- Ensure the correct post is opened before attempting to reply; a 404 error indicates the post URL is invalid.\n- Use 'go_back' and 'go_forward' carefully; the browser history may not reflect the intended navigation path if not managed correctly.\n- Verify that the 'Reply' link belongs to the intended comment (e.g., the first reply) before clicking.\n- The reply form includes a 'Comment' textbox which is marked as 'required' and must be filled.\n- Submit the reply by clicking the 'Post' button, not by pressing Enter or clicking elsewhere.\n- New replies may appear immediately after submission, often identified by a new username (e.g., 'MarvelsGrantMan136').\n- Navigate via the 'Forums' link from the home page if direct post URLs are unavailable."
